# commands.verbs - Dingus Quest Zero's verbs as data (the plan's "Verbs are data"): each verb, the words that say it,
# the action it makes (commands.actions' VB_*: actions.h) by the phrase's shape, the thing it takes when none is said,
# its own value for the game, the skill it tests and whether it's a long task.  The parser (games/dq0c, cmdmean.s)
# reads them compiled (sim/tools/commandwords.js's encode, a part of dq0c.dat, in a bank of dq0c's own) and gives the
# UI a command (hub.h's struct cmd: the action and its roles); sim/tools/commandwords.js is the host's reference.  A
# new phrasing is a word or a field here; a new verb a line; a new action a line of commands.actions and the game's
# code for it.
#
# [verbs]: a verb a line, its name, then its fields (name=value; none needed but one action):
#   alone=VB_*     the action when nothing follows the verb (no thing, no way): the thing's, its default filling it,
#                  if none's given
#   thing=VB_*     with a thing ("look at the wall")
#   way=VB_*       with a way and no thing ("look north"): the thing's, if none's given (the way where it lies)
#   WORD=VB_*      with a thing, that word straight after the verb ("look through the window", "look around the
#                  corner"): a preposition's own meaning for the verb
#   unsaid=        the thing when none is said: place (where the character is), last (the last thing named), near
#                  (the last thing named, else the things near: which, asked; none, said so), front (what's in
#                  front), target (the target, else the nearest foe), hand (what's in hand), none (it must be said)
#   aux=           the verb's own value for the game (struct cmd's aux): the things' request it is (IO_*), the
#                  denizens' sway (SW_*), what a blow strikes with (SK_*), an ally's request (OR_*)
#   skill=         the skill it tests (rs.h's P_*: the referee's)
#   task=          a long task, of its kind (hub.h's LT_*: interruptible, "stop" ends it)
#
# [words]: a word (or words: a verb of several, matched before one of one) = the verb it says, as a line's first;
# each also as the root its alias gives (commands.aliases: "peer" is look's, "attack" fight's).  A line that begins
# with none is a way, or a thing, alone: going there (move's).

[verbs]
move        way=VB_MOVE_DIRECTION thing=VB_MOVE_TOWARD alone=VB_MOVE_DIRECTION unsaid=none task=LT_WALK
enter       thing=VB_ENTER unsaid=front
approach    thing=VB_APPROACH_OBJECT unsaid=none task=LT_WALK
look        alone=VB_OBSERVE_LOCALE thing=VB_OBSERVE_OBJECT way=VB_OBSERVE_DIRECTION through=VB_OBSERVE_THROUGH around=VB_OBSERVE_AROUND for=VB_FIND_OBJECT in=VB_OBSERVE_IN into=VB_OBSERVE_IN inside=VB_OBSERVE_IN on=VB_OBSERVE_IN unsaid=place skill=P_NOTICE_SIGHT
examine     alone=VB_EXAMINE_LOCALE thing=VB_EXAMINE_OBJECT unsaid=place skill=P_APPRAISE
search      thing=VB_SEARCH unsaid=place skill=P_SEARCH task=LT_SEARCH
